---
title: Sheet-pan gnocchi with sausage and broccoli rabe
servings: 4
tags: [italian, pork, sheet-pan, weeknight]
cuisine: italian
time: 50 minutes
source: Sheet-Pan Gnocchi With Sausage and Broccoli Rabe by Kelli Solomon, Serious Eats, https://www.seriouseats.com/gnocchi-sheet-pan-dinner-recipe-11720560
nutrition:
  calories: 682 kcal
  fat: 40 g
  saturated fat: 12 g
  carbohydrates: 56 g
  sugar: 9 g
  protein: 27 g
  fiber: 7 g
  sodium: 1215 mg
---

Put a #baking sheet{} on a rack in the lower middle of the oven and heat it to
425°F (220°C).

In a #large bowl{}, toss the @gnocchi{12%oz}(one package), @onion{1}(halved, cut into 3/4 inch slices), @olive oil{2%tbsp}, @salt{1%tsp},
@red pepper flakes{1/2%tsp}, @fennel seeds{1/2%tsp} and
@black pepper{1/2%tsp}.

Spread the gnocchi on the hot sheet. Pinch the @Italian sausage{12%oz}(casings removed) into 1 inch pieces and dot them between the gnocchi.

Roast ~{30%minutes}, stirring halfway, until the sausage is cooked and
everything is browned and crisp.

Meanwhile, in the same bowl, rub the @broccoli rabe{10%oz}(trimmed, cut into 1 1/2 inch pieces) with @cherry tomatoes{8%oz}(halved), @garlic{4%cloves}(grated),
@lemon zest{1%tsp}, @salt{1/2%tsp} and @olive oil{2%tbsp}.

Scatter over the gnocchi and roast ~{6-10%minutes}, until the greens and
tomatoes are tender.

Stir in the @lemon juice{2%tbsp} and @parmesan cheese{3%tbsp}, and serve at
once with more parmesan.
